GROUND
Logical Ground Seqment sends Start_File_Transfer message to Command and 
    Data Handling (CDH) subsystem (i.e. host).

HOST
Host sends the Payload_X (emulator) using the Start_File_Transfer message
    with direction = upload. 

PAYLOAD
Payload_X recieves the Start_File_Transfer message. Then sends the ACK command with
    id of the Start_File_Transfer message

Payload_X starts recieving File Packets
// POTENTIAL FAULT INJECTION
* Recieving missing Packets
* Recieving out of order Packets
* Not recieving anything
* Taking too long to recieve files

HOST
Host recieves ACK message with Start_File_Transfer message_ID.
Host polls until Payload sends SFTP Transfer Completes, start recieving Packets
while (File_Transfer_Complete_Status.SFTP_status == 0)
    if (File_Transfer_Time >= File_Transfer_Timeout){
        Resend_Last_response for message_ID File_Transfer_Complete_Status
        // Use of timeout flag here is to verify if that the 
        if (timeout_flag){
            Send Return_to_Idle with message_ID=Start_File_Transfer
            Wait for ACK from payload
            // POSSIBLE FAULT INJECTION
            * No ACK knowledge message (Unless we always believe that the 
                ACK message can never fail)
        }
        timeout_flag = 1;
        File_Transfer_Time = 0;
    }
    if (SFTP_status = 1){
        // Fault response
        break;
    }


PAYLOAD
Payload_X completes the file transfer and send the File_Transfer_Complete_Status 
    message with SFTP_status = 0 (for success) or SFTP_status = 1 (for failure) 

HOST
Host starts sending space vehicle telemerty to the ground system.